course: dictionary
lesson: 1609
title: Compound words: cheeseburger
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cheeseburger is a compound word: two smaller words joined together, cheese and burger. When you know the parts, you can often work out the whole. «She ordered a cheeseburger and a small bag of chips.» Cheese plus burger tells you it is a burger with cheese on it.
explain: Sometimes the parts of a word lead you the wrong way. «Hamburger comes from Hamburg, a city in Germany, not from ham.» People split the word into ham and burger, and that made a guess that is not true. Then they made cheeseburger and veggie burger from the same pattern. When the clues mislead you, check the history.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. A cheeseburger is a hamburger with a slice of melted cheese on top of the meat patty, served in a bun. If your meaning fits the sentence and still makes sense, you are probably right.
fact: A cheeseburger is a hamburger with a slice of melted cheese on top of the meat patty.
fact: A cheeseburger is served in a bun.
fact: «Hamburger» comes from Hamburg, a city in Germany, not from ham.
fact: Related words: burger, hamburger, veggie burger.
fact: In health lessons, cheeseburgers are high in fat and salt, so they are fine as a treat but not every day.
exercise: «She ordered a cheeseburger and a small bag of chips.» What is a cheeseburger? | A bowl of soup with bread | *A hamburger with a slice of melted cheese on top, served in a bun | A cake filled with cheese | A sandwich with no meat
exercise: «The cheeseburger was hot, and the cheese had melted over the meat.» What does melted mean here? | Wrapped in paper | Frozen solid | *Turned soft and runny because of heat | Cut into small cubes
exercise: Which two smaller words make up cheeseburger? | cheesebur and ger | ch and eeseburger | *cheese and burger | chees and eburger
test: «Hamburger comes from Hamburg, a city in Germany, not from ham.» Why do some people think hamburger comes from ham? | Because ham is a city in Germany | Because hamburgers are always made of ham | Because Hamburg is a food | *Because they split the word into ham and burger, which is a wrong guess
test: In health lessons, why is a cheeseburger an example of food to eat only sometimes? | It is made of wood | It is only sold in the winter | It has no taste at all | *It is high in fat and salt, so it is fine as a treat but not every day
exam: Tom says a cheeseburger is a cake. What is the correct meaning? | A salad with cheese on top | *A hamburger with a slice of melted cheese on top of the meat patty, served in a bun | A bread roll with no filling | A cake made with cheese
